  "sale_events": [],
  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 11 November 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nPrivately elevated above Mairangi Bay, this impressive 306sqm (more or less) architecturally designed weatherboard home captures breathtaking panoramic views.\r\n\r\nBuilt in 2009 and positioned to enjoy all-day sun, this beautifully maintained residence offers exceptional space, privacy and flexibility for growing families, extended family or those who love to entertain.\r\n\r\nGenerous living spaces span two levels, including an open-plan kitchen, dining and family area, and two additional family living areas. Expansive decks provide the perfect setting for outdoor entertaining while enjoying the spectacular coastal outlook.\r\n\r\nProperty Features:\r\n\r\n• 306sqm (more or less) architecturally designed weatherboard home\r\n• Six generous bedrooms, including a master suite with walk-in wardrobe and ensuite\r\n• Two bathrooms and four toilets\r\n• Spacious open-plan kitchen, dining and family living\r\n• Formal lounge plus two additional family living areas\r\n• Double internal-access garage and ample off-street parking\r\n• Private cul-de-sac setting with elevated Gulf views\r\n• Close to Mairangi Bay Village, beaches, parks and coastal walkways\r\n• Convenient motorway access and Constellation Bus Station\r\n• Zoned for Mairangi Bay School, Murrays Bay Intermediate, Rangitoto College and Westlake Girls High School\r\n\r\nCombining panoramic sea views, generous family accommodation and exceptional privacy, this is a rare opportunity to secure a substantial home in one of the North Shore’s sought-after coastal suburbs.\r\n\r\nEnjoy the space, embrace the views and make Mairangi Bay your home.",
